<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
{% comment %}
  Syndication feed for the Cloudscript LinkedIn Page, consumed by the Zapier "New Item in
  Feed" -> LinkedIn Pages "Create Company Update" Zap. Deliberately NOT advertised: no
  <link rel="alternate"> in default.html, no mention on /news/, so subscribers to the public
  Atom feed (news/feed.xml) never see the LinkedIn copy. It is still a public URL, so nothing
  confidential belongs in it.

  Each entry's body is the post's `linkedin:` front matter (copy written for the LinkedIn
  audience), falling back to `description` when a post has none. A post with `linkedin: false`
  is omitted entirely (use this for retrodated or housekeeping posts that must not be
  announced). The same text is emitted as <summary> and <content> so the Zap can map
  whichever field Zapier surfaces. Zapier keys on <id>, so editing a published post does not
  re-post it.

  The post's `image:` (the same file as og:image) is emitted twice per entry, as an Atom
  enclosure link and as a Media RSS <media:thumbnail>, because LinkedIn's API does not scrape
  og:image for posts created through it (confirmed 7 Sep 2026: Post Inspector showed the
  image, the Zapier-created post did not).

  Zap configuration as shipped (7 Sep 2026), LinkedIn Pages "Create Company Update":
    Update Content = Description + "\n\nFull release notes: " + ID
    Image Type     = post_media          Image = Link Enclosure
    Media URL, Preview Title, Preview Description = empty
  Zapier flattens the two <link> elements into one space-joined "Link" value, so the article
  URL must come from ID (= the post URL), never from Link. An image post and a link card
  cannot be combined (LinkedIn API: "DataMap should have no more than one entry for a union
  type"), which is why the URL travels in the text and the card is not used.
{% endcomment %}
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/">
  <title>CloudScript.io News (LinkedIn syndication)</title>
  <id>{{ "/news/linkedin.xml" | absolute_url }}</id>
  <link href="{{ "/news/" | absolute_url }}"/>
  <link rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" href="{{ "/news/linkedin.xml" | absolute_url }}"/>
  <updated>{% if site.posts.size > 0 %}{{ site.posts.first.date | date_to_xmlschema }}{% else %}{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}{% endif %}</updated>
  <author><name>CloudScript.io</name></author>
{% for post in site.posts limit: 20 %}{% if post.linkedin == false %}{% continue %}{% endif %}{% if post.linkedin %}{% assign body = post.linkedin | strip %}{% else %}{% assign body = post.description | strip %}{% endif %}
  <entry>
    <title>{{ post.title | xml_escape }}</title>
    <id>{{ post.url | absolute_url }}</id>
    <link href="{{ post.url | absolute_url }}"/>
{% if post.image %}{% assign img = post.image | absolute_url %}{% if post.image contains ".png" %}{% assign mime = "image/png" %}{% else %}{% assign mime = "image/jpeg" %}{% endif %}    <link rel="enclosure" type="{{ mime }}" href="{{ img }}"/>
    <media:thumbnail url="{{ img }}"/>
{% endif %}    <published>{{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</published>
    <updated>{{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
    <summary type="text">{{ body | xml_escape }}</summary>
    <content type="text">{{ body | xml_escape }}</content>
  </entry>
{% endfor %}
</feed>
